 [{:title
   "CLI --embedding-version flag is still accepted but silently dropped by the closed query/search schema",
   :file "src/epiphany/infra/main.clj",
   :detail
   "`search-options` still advertises and parses `--embedding-version VER` (main.clj lines 294-296). The old `build-search-request` (deleted in 7977f2a) passed it through to `hs/search`, which uses it as a real semantic filter (hybrid_search.clj:167,189,198 → lucene.clj:250-251 applies a FILTER clause on embedding_version). The new `run-search` candidate omits `:embedding-version`, and the closed `query/search` schema (law/commands.clj:24-33) has no such key — so `ep search --embedding-version 3 -m semantic foo` now silently returns semantically-unfiltered results, and the capability can't even be re-added to the candidate without a schema change. Undocumented behavior change (the card documents only the status/:local and inbox-decide changes) and it violates the repo's 'never silent' boundary rule: the flag should either be threaded through the schema or removed/rejected.",
   :severity "should-fix",
   :card "eng-017g2",
   :lens "correctness",
   :survives true,
   :reasons
   ["Every element of the claim verifies against the actual code and history. (1) main.clj:294-296 still advertises and parses --embedding-version in search-options. (2) git show 7977f2a~1:src/epiphany/infra/main.clj (lines 368-369) confirms the pre-card build-search-request threaded (:embedding-version opts) into the search request, and hybrid_search.clj:167/189/198 passes it to the knn-search port where lucene.clj:250-251 applies a real BooleanClause FILTER on embedding_version — so this was a working semantic filter, not dead code. (3) The new run-search (main.clj:391-398) builds the candidate with only query/mode/limit/path-prefix/ref, and law/commands.clj:24-33 query/search is [:map {:closed true}] with no embedding-version key, so the flag is now parsed and silently ignored — unfiltered semantic results are returned to a user who asked for a version filter. (4) The change is not grandfathered: it was introduced by this card's own commit 7977f2a. (5) It is not documented as an accepted tradeoff: the card's IMPLEMENTED comment explicitly enumerates two behavior changes (status/:local parity, inbox-decide phantom-decision hardening) and is silent on this one; no later comment or deferral record exists. (6) It is in-scope: the card owns the run-search rewiring and the query/search vocabulary, and embedding-version is semantic intent (a real result filter), not a surface concern like format/profile/index-dir that the schema docstring legitimately excludes. The parity argument does not save it — HTTP never had the flag, but the seam's purpose is to lift capabilities into the shared vocabulary or reject unknown intent loudly, not to keep accepting a flag and dropping it, which is exactly the 'never a silent fallback' boundary rule the repo states. A wrong-result silent drop on a shipped CLI flag, trivially fixable (add :embedding-version to the schema filters or remove/reject the flag), is a legitimate should-fix that gates promotion."
    "Every element of the claim verified against the code. Pre-card (7977f2a^), main.clj's build-search-request (lines 368-369) threaded :embedding-version into hs/search, which applies it as a real FILTER clause (domain/hybrid_search.clj:167,189,198 -> infra/adapters/lucene.clj:250-251, mirrored in the in-memory adapter). Post-card, search-options still advertises and parses `--embedding-version VER` (main.clj:294-296), but run-search's candidate (main.clj:391-398) omits it, and the card's new closed query/search schema (law/commands.clj:24-33) has no such key — parse-opts succeeds, so the flag is accepted and silently ignored; `ep search --embedding-version 3 -m semantic foo` returns semantically unfiltered results with no error. This is a behavior regression on the search command, which this card explicitly rewired, caused by the card's own candidate construction and schema design — squarely in delivered scope, not grandfathered code (git history shows the threading existed until this card's commit deleted build-search-request). The card's IMPLEMENTED comment and commit message enumerate the accepted behavior changes — status/:local parity and inbox-decide phantom-decision hardening — and do not mention embedding-version, so it is not a documented/accepted tradeoff; nor is it in Non-goals. The silence directly violates the repo's explicit boundary posture (schema header: surface concerns like format/profile/index-dir are excluded, but embedding-version is a result-set-changing semantic filter, not a surface concern — law/ports.clj:139 even carries it as a port-level query parameter). The fix is trivial either direction (drop the flag from search-options, or add an optional :embedding-version key to the schema so execute-search's (dissoc command :command/name) passthrough restores the filter), but leaving an advertised no-op flag on a covered command is a real, in-scope defect gating review->done under the repo's never-silent rule."]}
