   :reasons
   ["The string is present (lines 23-25, not 19-21 as claimed), but the finding fails every gating test. (1) Grandfathered, deliberate pattern: the identical credential pre-exists in test/epiphany/infra/adapters/mongo_test.clj:32, introduced by commit 0a99597 (ENG-001A era) — not by this card. The new file reuses the established integration-test fixture so the differential suite hits the same local Mongo as the pre-existing harness. (2) Documented: the card's IMPLEMENTED comment explicitly records 'Mongo via MONGODB_URI-style test URI already used by mongo_test' — the reuse was a disclosed decision, and the card's Non-goals carve out infrastructure-topology work ('No CI-topology work beyond making the suite runnable'; CI wiring is ENG-017J). (3) Out of scope: the card's Scope is registry-driven write-path validation plus law-suite parity; consolidating test credentials or moving to env-var-driven URIs belongs to the profile/config boundary (US-000C) or ENG-017J, and fixing it 'properly' would require touching mongo_test.clj, a file outside this card's delivered change. (4) Too minor to gate: this is a localhost:27017 dev-only credential for an Epiphany-owned throwaway test database that teardown drops — not a production secret; AGENTS.md's 'never hardcode' legislates the application profile/config boundary, and two prior skeptic passes on this identical finding (journaled in .ημ/runs/eng-017e-017g2-review/journal.jsonl) already refuted it on the same grounds. Not promotion-gating."
    "Factually the string is there (observations_mongo_test.clj:25), but this does not survive as a promotion-gating finding for ENG-017E. (1) Deliberate and documented: the card's IMPLEMENTED comment (line 126) explicitly records 'Mongo via MONGODB_URI-style test URI already used by mongo_test' — the implementer consciously reused the established test-connection pattern rather than introducing a new practice, and the reviewer-facing card history contains no objection to it. (2) Grandfathered pattern, not a new class of violation: the identical URI was committed in mongo_test.clj:32 by 0a99597, long before this card's commit 91ab60f; this card changed zero credential policy, it added one integration test file that must reach the same local dev Mongo the existing suite already reaches. (3) Scope: the card's scope is registry-driven write validation + law-suite parity against real Mongo; connection-config centralization is owned by the profile/config boundary card (US-000C) for application runtime, and no card has yet chartered a shared test-config helper — demanding one here is scope creep the card never promised. (4) Not promotion-gating: the 'credential' is a localhost-only dev database login (127.0.0.1) for a throwaway test database; the marginal blast radius of a second copy in a test file is one line, and any rotation must already touch the pre-existing copy. The right disposition is a hygiene chore to introduce a shared test-URI helper covering both files, not blocking review→done of a card whose acceptance criteria (law suite green against real Mongo, differential parity) are unaffected. Fix belongs in a separate card, not this promotion."]}
