   "New law-suite test file adds a second hardcoded copy of the MongoDB credentials",
   :file "test/epiphany/law_suite/observations_mongo_test.clj",
   :detail
   "Lines 16-18 embed the full URI with password (mongodb://openplanner:GamG7Ly2g7eyMJoIa-4zS17eAUlWiUup@...) in a second test file. AGENTS.md legislates 'never hardcode, never commit credentials' for Mongo connection settings. The identical string pre-exists in mongo_test.clj (the card explicitly reuses that pattern), so this extends rather than introduces the violation — but the right move was to share one fixture constant (or read MONGODB_URI, which connect! already supports) instead of duplicating the secret.",
   :severity "nit",
